# DialKey — performance gate

**Rule Rev.1** — 2026-09-13 (DialKey)

**Before opening a version-bump PR** (or adding `ship` to the chat title),
measure and **append rows to `docs/spec.md` §10**. Do not skip because the
change “looks cheap.” Docs-only work with no rev bump does not need this gate.

## What to run

Release build. Tray only (no Settings / typing UI). Isolated work dir with
minimal `settings.json` **and** `slots.json` (so first-run Settings does not
open).

```powershell
.\scripts\measure-startup.ps1 -ExePath <isolated\dialkey.exe> -WorkDir <same folder> -Runs 10 -Footprint
```

Copy the release exe into a writable folder first (`dist/stage` can auto-open
Settings). **n = 10** (warmup 1, not counted). Record **mean**, **unbiased SD**
\(\hat\sigma=\sqrt{\mathrm{SS}/(n-1)}\), min–max, and the **raw sample list**.

| Metric | Spec table |
|---|---|
| Startup → log `ready` (ms) | §10 startup |
| Idle **Private Bytes** (canonical) + Working Set | §10 resident footprint |

Keep old rows. Goal: Private stays in the low single-digit MB.

## Comparing two builds

Same n=10, α = 0.05. `scripts/measure-stats.ps1`. Print:

1. **Normality** — Shapiro–Wilk W vs Wcrit(0.05) (n=5..12)
2. **Equal variance** — two-sided F-test
3. **Mean difference** — Student t if F not rejected, otherwise Welch

If Shapiro–Wilk rejects (often Private Bytes at 0.01 MB rounding), still print
F/t but do not treat p as a strong claim.

Focus-path PRs also run `scripts/measure-compare-n10.ps1`.

## Order

Implement → spec behaviour → **§10 n=10 + σ̂** → PR → chat title `Rev.{version} ship`.
